            "description": "Watch Northampton vs Plymouth highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 2, 2026. In a pulsating League One fixture held on 2 May 2026 , Northampton and Plymouth locked horns in a clash defined by rapid momentum shifts and high-stakes drama. A whirlwind first half The match exploded into life early on, with Elliott List finding the net in the 13th minute after a setup from Michael Jacobs . Barely five minutes later, Michael Jacobs turned from provider to scorer, doubling the lead with assistance from Nesta Guinness-Walker . Plymouth refused to crumble, pulling a goal back in the 28th minute through Lorent Tolaj , assisted by Joe Edwards . The visitors completed their fightback just before half-time when Malachi Boateng slotted home a Lorent Tolaj delivery to level the scores at the interval. Numerical advantage and the decider The second half saw tempers fray as both sides sought control, leading to a flurry of yellow cards. The decisive turning point arrived in the 62nd minute when Plymouth defender Conor McCarthy was sent off after picking up a second yellow card. The numerical advantage eventually told in the 74th minute, as Brendan Sarpong-Wiredu struck the decisive blow for Northampton , following an assist by Xavier Amaechi . Despite a series of late substitutions to inject fresh legs, the score remained unchanged, cementing a dramatic finish in front of the supporters.",
